     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §105, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8328\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales\nwithin a certain distance of a church\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo permit the licensure of a liquor store at a certain location within\n200 feet of a place of worship.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- Amends subdivision 3 of section 105 of the alcoholic beverage\ncontrol law to permit for the sale of alcohol at a property within the\ncity of Glens Falls, which is within 200 feet of a place of worship.\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would permit the State Liquor Authority to license a\nproposed liquor store within the city of Glens Falls.  The would-be\nstore's location, as measured by the SLA, is 196 feet from a place of\nworship.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
